{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01SJ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-quasi-affine}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ad22a7f5ef045e7fae2292d4e398d95e5f7b0399d950bd7c6ada064feea13628", "source_text": "Quasi-affine morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aaa34838781ae899ccf3deeccb5a409fbc6d52c8fd9a3b74337382e53b43e132", "unit_id": "tag:01SJ:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01SJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{properties-definition-quasi-affine}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2cdd54c91172842da7935e351b2e537dfc65808da525fec53dd82898c278104", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7dbc4a74d7c07145d352c75cf8278c9557dff89f48a8a67614e5cbfb6d24f31b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that a scheme <MATH_0001> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-affine<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if it is quasi-compact\nand isomorphic to an open subscheme of an affine scheme, see\nProperties, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8c3ce428f66ecc53730c92619d5ceff0ece1e19cde484f7d7c36669e8f3136bb", "unit_id": "tag:01SJ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01SJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-quasi-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:85b21a83f7d43ff3ffd7b2bca2e17a0df7f7e67f50faf874aeda64e715735fd1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8698d6b2be2161f75bff85460c1b8899b6bdea36543d3ceae7686f21f2ad2148", "source_text": "A morphism of schemes <MATH_0001> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-affine<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the\ninverse image of every affine open of <MATH_0002> is a quasi-affine scheme.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:89f2d44ee6432471b3fb6cf61dc7fa0b08d40472fcf6d6542c2e47e71f60acb4", "unit_id": "tag:01SK:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01SJ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-affine-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9089436a1abb86a9217de36e94aecad8968c73ca801c752dc74c0097623d6c32", "source_text": "A quasi-affine morphism is separated and quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1596c282c0fb11a6e6a5c41c0863476f4c028e40346dec4d5cf7ca6dbba8064e", "unit_id": "tag:01SL:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01SJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\subset S$", "MATH_0003": "$f^{-1}(U)$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f^{-1}(U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-characterize-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b09cc5c0a56705f07ff0f90fb640ab36bd70eb567e474fc44c0f026604cc671", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:68a3481e87dbeb4fba1674e0fb3c78b95902e673e2b330509e389b8b2b7dfb64", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be quasi-affine.\nQuasi-compactness is immediate from\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an affine open. If we can show that\n<MATH_0003> is a separated scheme, then <MATH_0004> is separated\n(Schemes, Lemma <REF_0002>\nshows that being separated is local on the base).\nBy assumption <MATH_0005> is isomorphic to an open subscheme\nof an affine scheme. An affine scheme is separated and hence\nevery open subscheme of an affine scheme is separated as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0e8e1460ddce2a26c4e47bc19f90ee60a2c69ddfe60ccee5dd30c821a7e7c5c7", "unit_id": "tag:01SL:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01SJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$S = \\bigcup W_j$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}(W_j)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\ar[rr] \\ar[rd] & & \\underline{\\Spec}_S(\\mathcal{A}) \\ar[dl] \\\\\n& S &\n}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{A} = f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{constructions-lemma-canonical-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-quasi-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d3edb4f156673d908e07cbc95bf596725950bb23e91b6ff021f7aafc42819b45", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1331673d25c2c0a64956ce87b92c4867e45ee3932abb40d9022d7387a445f601", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The morphism <MATH_0002> is quasi-affine.\n<STRUCT_0003> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0003>\nsuch that each <MATH_0004> is quasi-affine.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists a quasi-coherent sheaf of <MATH_0005>-algebras\n<MATH_0006> and a quasi-compact open immersion\n<MATH_0007>\nover <MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0005> Same as in (3) but with <MATH_0009>\nand the horizontal arrow the canonical morphism of\nConstructions, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:978233598b059b648fbb38bbf33ab2ac93148b00236561540dd97f0f65d5e9a1", "unit_id": "tag:01SM:statement"}
